<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dominion of India</h1><p class="st-meta">1947 CE – 1950 CE · capital New Delhi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Independent India's first constitutional form, a Commonwealth dominion that integrated the princely states and drafted the constitution of the republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence-act-1947">Indian Independence Act</a> of 1947, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj</a> was partitioned, and on 15 August 1947 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> was created with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru">Jawaharlal Nehru</a> as prime minister. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-mountbatten">Lord Mountbatten</a> stayed on as Governor-General until 1948, succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/c-rajagopalachari">C. Rajagopalachari</a>, the only Indian to hold the post.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dominion confronted partition violence and refugee resettlement, and fought the first war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-pakistan">Dominion of Pakistan</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vallabhbhai-patel">Vallabhbhai Patel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/v-p-menon">V. P. Menon</a> integrated more than five hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, using force against Hyderabad in 1948. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a> was assassinated in January 1948. A Constituent Assembly chaired in drafting by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/b-r-ambedkar">B. R. Ambedkar</a> wrote the new constitution.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a> came into force on 26 January 1950, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> a sovereign republic within the Commonwealth and ending the British monarch's role as head of state. The dominion was succeeded by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-india">Republic of India</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dominion-of-india.jpg" alt="Dominion of India" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1947 CE – 1950 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Delhi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jawaharlal Nehru, Lord Mountbatten, C. Rajagopalachari</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hindi, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Union of India (1947-1950), India (dominion)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1948&amp;focus=dominion-of-india" aria-label="Dominion of India on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: where Dominion of India lay"><image href="/maps/globes/g090n30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4048 5065L4869 5635M4048 5065L4048 5065M4048 5065L4102 4827M4048 5065L3906 6734M4048 5065L4099 5276M4048 5065L4326 5441M4048 5065L3509 5531M4048 5065L3995 5149M4048 5065L3930 5197M4048 5065L4066 6025M4048 5065L3895 6425M4048 5065L3936 4580M4048 5065L3690 5560M4048 5065L4019 5521M4048 5065L3725 6039M4048 5065L3436 5435M4048 5065L4065 6599M4048 5065L3690 5429M4048 5065L4183 5063M4048 5065L4886 5209M4048 5065L3691 5338M4048 5065L4457 5386M4048 5065L4923 5324M4048 5065L3476 5591M4048 5065L3651 5394M4048 5065L3709 5599M4048 5065L5099 5526M4048 5065L4046 4832M4048 5065L3646 5553M4048 5065L4010 4721M4048 5065L3640 5892M4048 5065L4057 4800M4048 5065L5306 5437M4048 5065L4072 4900M4048 5065L4052 4815M4048